            <div xml:id="d293">

                <pb facs="0587" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg491"/>

                <head>No. 291.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Schenck to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-12-12"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 12, 1873</date>.
                        (Received December 27.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 534.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the correspondence which was
                    communicated to you in my No. 453, relating to the privileges to be extended by
                    Her Majesty’s government or certain of her colonial governments to the
                    expedition to be sent next year from the United States for the purpose of
                    observing the transit of Venus, I have now to transmit to you a copy of another
                    note received from Lord Granville on that subject. His lordship writes to inform
                    me that there has been communicated to him from the secretary of state for the
                    colonies a memorandum from the governor of Tasmania, stating that instructions
                    will be given for the admission free of duty and wharfage of all instruments,
                    &amp;c., to be used by the expedition, and that a suitable site will be assigned
                    for making the observations.</p>
                <p>You will doubtless desire to have this information to convey to the Secretary of
                    the Navy.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ROBT. C. SCHENCK.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d293-a1.xml" xpointer="d293-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
